# Test: interface backend vpp refuses a firewall table producer without firewall backend vpp.
# Question: does `ze config validate` refuse `control-plane-protection` (copp)
#           under `interface backend vpp` when no `firewall` block sets
#           `firewall backend vpp`?
#           A unit test cannot prove `ze config validate` activates the
#           secondary `firewall` selector when a registered `FollowsSelector`
#           producer (`copp`) is present without a `firewall` root.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-3 -- an active firewall
#            table producer under `interface backend vpp` requires `firewall
#            backend vpp`, refusing with `control-plane-protection` and
#            `set firewall backend vpp`.
# PREVENTS: CoPP silently programming kernel tables through the default
#           firewall backend while VPP forwards the packets.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	backend vpp;
}
control-plane-protection {
	bgp {
		rate 100/second;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=control-plane-protection
expect=stdout:contains=set firewall backend vpp
